    "result_text": "The build succeeds and all tests pass. Here's a summary of the change I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` endpoint now accepts an optional `birthDate` (ISO date) and the owner responses expose a derived `ageBand` (`MINOR` / `ADULT` / `SENIOR`), computed from `birthDate` against the owner's `registrationDate`.\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 the DTOs are generated from this spec:\n   - Added optional `birthDate` (`format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` request schema.\n   - Added read-only `ageBand` (string) to the `Owner` response schema.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `birthDate` (`LocalDate`, `birth_date` column) field with getter/setter, so the value survives create \u2192 `SaveOwner` \u2192 `GET /owners/{id}` reload.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 MapStruct maps `birthDate` in/out by name automatically; added an `ageBand(owner)` helper wired via `@Mapping`. It returns `null` when `birthDate` is absent, otherwise bands the whole-year age (`Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate)`): `<18 \u2192 MINOR`, `18\u201364 \u2192 ADULT`, `65+ \u2192 SENIOR`. It falls back to `LocalDate.now()` defensively, though the create pipeline always sets `registrationDate`.\n\n4. **`src/main/resources/db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in every dialect (tests run on hsqldb).\n\nNo OfficeFloor YAML/function changes were needed: `ValidateOwnerFields` republishes the whole `OwnerFieldsDto` (now carrying `birthDate`) and `BuildOwner`'s `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)` copies it onto the entity.\n\nThe provided acceptance test (`coreDerivesAgeBand`: `birthDate` `1990-01-01`, default registration date `2026-09-04` \u2192 `ADULT`) and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
